            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "as Hasbrouck's information share isolates the fraction of price discovery attributable to a given venue's order flow, our  $ \\hat{\\lambda}_{it} $ estimates isolate the fraction of a stock's monthly price variation attributable to signed order flow as opposed to noise-driven trading. This connection motivates a natural robustness check in our empirical design (Section 9): decomposing realized return variance into a signed-order-flow component and a residual component, in the spirit of an information-share calculation applied to a single market over time rather than across markets at a point in time.",
